From 4824de7723cf3445d0445d167a983b603c96e4b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yulun Zeng <yulunz@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:27:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/32] [DevTools] Gate browser-side network overrides on
 MayAttachToURL

Network.setExtraHTTPHeaders overrides (extra headers, Referer override,
cache / service worker bypass) were applied to browser-initiated
requests without checking whether the session's client may access the
request URL. For navigations, the overrides were applied before
OnNavigationRequestWillBeSent() force-detached sessions whose client
fails MayAttachToURL(), so a chrome.debugger extension could inject
headers and a spoofed Referer into credentialed requests to restricted
origins such as the Chrome Web Store.

Skip sessions whose client may not attach to the request URL when
applying network overrides to navigations, WebSocket handshakes and
worker main script requests. Redirects and renderer-initiated
subresource requests are handled separately.

